<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθᾰγ-ίζω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>: 
			Ion.
		
		fut.
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ-αγιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.86
				</span></i>
			:—<i>devote, dedicate</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκροθίνια θεῶν ὅτεῳ δή</span> l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήττῃ πυρούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					566
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lys.</u>
				238
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				120a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				319.13
			</span></i>, etc.; esp. of a burnt offering, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμιήματα κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.130
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πυρί</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				47
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐπὶ πύρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.167
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τοῦ βωμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.183
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρκεύθου ξύλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					2.10.5
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.40
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>make offerings</i> to the dead, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Luct.</u>
				9
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.190
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταγιζ-</span> Pap., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθαγνιζ-</span> codd.), <i><span class="en">
				558
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθαγνιζ-</span> codd.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
			<i>burn</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταγιζομένου τοῦ καρποῦ
				τοῦ ἐπιβαλλομένου [ἐπὶ τὸ πῦρ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.202
			</span></i>; esp. <i>burn</i> a dead body, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				σῶμα τοῦ Καίσαρος ἐν ἀγορᾷ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Brut.</u>
				20
			</span></i>; so (as cj. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθήγνισαν</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ὅσων σπαράγματ᾽
				ἢ κύνες καθήγισαν</span> whose mangled bodies dogs
				<i>have buried</i>, i.e. <i>devoured</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1081
			</span></i> (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ ἄγους ἐκόμισαν</span>,
			Sch.).</div>
